{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"reasoning","text":"Now the legend is completely clear:\n1. **EuZn1.8Cd0.2Sb2** — red filled circle, with a line\n2. **YbCd1.6Zn0.4Sb2** — blue star, with a line (note: blue STAR, not circle!)\n3. **EuZn2Sb2** — open circle (black), with a line\n4. **EuCd2Sb2** — filled circle (black), with a line\n5. **YbCd2Sb2** — open star (black), with a line\n6. **YbZn2Sb2** — filled star (black), with a line\n\nWait, that makes 6 series! Let me count again from the legend image:\n1. EuZn1.8Cd0.2Sb2 (red filled circle)\n2. YbCd1.6Zn0.4Sb2 (blue star)\n3. EuZn2Sb2 (open circle)\n4. EuCd2Sb2 (filled circle)\n5. YbCd2Sb2 (open star)\n6. YbZn2Sb2 (filled star)\n\nYes, 6 series. And looking at the left crop, the data curves from top to bottom at low T are: red filled circle, blue star, open circle, filled circle, open star, filled star.\n\nAt the left end (low T), the markers are dense. In the left crop I can see 6 rows of markers: red circles, blue stars, open circles, filled circles, open stars, filled stars.\n\nTherefore, in the previous summary \"4 black markers on the right, but 3 on the left\" — that was probably talking about the black ones among them: open circle, filled circle, open star, filled star = 4 black series. At the left end, the open markers (open circle, open star) may overlap with the filled markers, or may be hard to see.\n\nNow, about the x-axis: the data is from about 300K to about 700K. Calibration: pixel_x 100.8 → 300, pixel_x 326.85 → 700. So pixels per K = (326.85-100.8)/(700-300) = 226.05/400 = 0.565125 px/K.\n\nY-axis: pixel_y 222.7 → 0.0, pixel_y 19.95 → 1.4. So pixels per zT = (222.7-19.95)/1.4 = 202.75/1.4 = 144.821 px per 1 zT.\n\nNow, the number of data points: the x values look like they are at regular intervals. From the left crop, markers appear roughly every ~35-40 pixels? The x-axis is 300 to 700 K. Looking at the markers in the left crop: at the left end, markers are lined up at positions