black extent ≥4 within radius 5 (stars: 5 arms; circles: all directions ~2.5-3.5)\n   Actually, filled star vs filled circle: the star's maxrad is ~5-6, the circle's maxrad is ~3.5. And the star's meanrad is ~3.5-4 vs the circle's ~2.8.\n   Open star: ring-shaped arms + white center. Open circle: thin ring + white center.\nStep 5: Assign markers to x positions (snap to the nearest of the 21 x grid points), group into series, and verify that each series has 21 points.\n\nPotential problem: where a marker overlaps with a line of the same color (a black line passes through the black marker) — the density is high, no problem. Where a marker overlaps with the blue/red line — a black mask near a colored line is unaffected.\n\nStep 6: Convert pixel centers to data coordinates using the calibration.\n\nLet me write a comprehensive script. First, let me look at the right crop to understand the ordering at high T."}}
