ript that:\n1. Detects red centers (density peaks).\n2. Detects blue centers (density peaks).\n3. Detects filled black cores (erosion + components).\n4. Detects open marker holes (white components).\n5. Dumps everything with features; classifies; snaps to grid.\n\nThen compute data coordinates:\nT = 300 + (px - 100.8)/0.565125\nzT = (222.7 - py)/144.8214\n\nLet me write it."}}
