ar): x=101..298, 15 points\n5. EuCd₂Sb₂ (black filled circles): x=101..298, 15 points\n6. YbCd₂Sb₂ (black bottom star): x=101..326, 17 points\n\nWait, I need to double-check the x-range for each black curve. Let me reconsider.\n\nAt x=312, 326: only 2 black markers (96.0/82.7 upper, 162.7/155.8 lower).\n\nAt x=298: 4 black markers (97.1, 108.6, 125.4, 169.5).\n\nSo the 2 black curves that continue to x=326 are the top one (97.1→96.0→82.7) and the bottom one (169.5→162.7→155.8).\n\nTop black = open circle (EuZn₂Sb₂). Bottom black = bottom star (YbCd₂Sb₂).\n\nSo:\n- EuZn₂Sb₂ (open): x=101..326 (17 points)\n- YbCd₂Sb₂ (bottom star): x=101..326 (17 points)\n- YbZn₂Sb₂ (top star): x=101..298 (15 points)\n- EuCd₂Sb₂ (filled): x=101..298 (15 points)\n\nOK. Now let me extract the exact y for each point on each curve.\n\nThe challenge is at low T (x=101..~170) where the curves are crowded and some overlap. Let me carefully assign.\n\nLet me get clean per-column y values for all 6 curves (red, blue, black) and assign to curves.\n\nLet me write a comprehensive extraction. For each x in xgrid, I'll get the red, blue, and black marker y centers. Then assign black to the 4 curves based on rank/position, being careful about overlaps.\n\nLet me reconsider the black assignment at each x. I'll use the following logic:\n- At each x, sort black y values (ascending = top to bottom).\n- Map to curves based on the known ordering and x-range.\n\nOrdering (top to bottom) at a given x (where all 4 are present):\nrank 1 = EuZn₂Sb₂ (open)\nrank 2 = YbZn₂Sb₂ (top star)\nrank 3 = EuCd₂Sb₂ (filled)\nrank 4 = YbCd₂Sb₂ (bottom star)\n\nBut at low T some may overlap. Let me check the data:\n\nx=101: black [196.9, 210.7] (2 values). Expected 4. So 2 pairs are overlapping, or some curves aren't present.\nHmm. Let me reconsider.\n\nWait, maybe at x=101 not all 4 black curves are present. Let me reconsider. Actually, the issue is that at low T the 4 black curves are close together and the detector is merging them.\n\nLet me reconsider. At x=101 (lowest T), the 4 black curves should be at 4 different (but close) y values. The detector found 196.9 and 210.7. Maybe:\n- EuZn (open) and YbZn (top star) are merged around 196.9?\n- EuCd (filled) and YbCd (bottom star) are merged around 210.7?\n\nOr maybe the detector is just missing some.\n\nThis is really hard. Let me look at the leftmost column very carefully. Let me zoom in a lot on x=101, y=190..220.\n\nActually, let me reconsider my approach entirely. Given the difficulty, let me be pragmatic:\n\nFor the red and blue curves (already done, 15 and 17 points), let me re-extract cleanly to confirm.\n\nFor the 4 black curves, let me extract as best I can. Where markers overlap at low T, I'll use the visible marker centers and make a reasonable assignment.\n\nLet me get the exact per-column data one more time, very carefully, with good marker detection, and also output what shape each black marker is (to help with assignment).\n\nActually, let me reconsider. Let me look at the actual y values and try to fit smooth curves.\n\nLet me extract the black y values per column (cleaned) and print them. Then reason about the assignment.\n\nLet me reconsider the black data per column (excluding axis ~227):\nx=101: [196.9, 210.7]\nx=115: [191.3, 203.3, 216.3]\nx=128: [187.1, 199.4, 215.1]\nx=143: [180.0, 195.1, 213.0]\nx=157: [168.8, 172.7, 189.9, 211.4]\nx=171: [160.6, 165.3, 184.7, 209.2]\nx=185: [153.0, 179.0, 206.5]\nx=199: [144.7, 172.8, 203.6]\nx=213: [135.9, 166.5, 200.5]\nx=227: [126.8, 159.0, 196.3]\nx=241: [123.4, 151.9, 192.5]\nx=256: [115.0, 143.8, 187.0]\nx=270: [106.7, 131.3, 140.5, 181.8]\nx=284: [99.8, 120.8, 133.6, 175.6]\nx=298: [97.1, 108.6, 125.4, 169.5]\nx=312: [96.0, 162.7]\nx=326: [82.7, 155.8]\n\nNow, the 4 black curves (top to bottom): EuZn (open), YbZn (top star), EuCd (filled), YbCd (bottom star).\n\nLet me try to assign by tracking from high T (where it's clean) to low T.\n\nAt x=298 (clean, 4 values):\nE