s bottom).\n\nLet me do a clean blob detection that gives me (x, y, shape) for each black marker, then cluster.\n\nLet me write a robust detector:\n1. Mask the black.\n2. Detect blobs with connected components.\n3. For each blob, determine shape:\n   - Compute the \"hole\" (is there a white center?) → open circle vs filled\n   - Compute the aspect and the number of \"points\" → star vs circle\n4. Get the centroid (x, y).\n\nLet me implement shape classification:\n- Open circle: ring, has a hole in the middle, roughly circular.\n- Filled circle: disk, no hole, circular, high fill ratio.\n- Star: 5 points, lower fill ratio than a circle (within its bounding box), no hole.\n\nLet me compute for each blob:\n- Fill ratio = blob pixels / bounding box area\n- Hole: check if the center pixel is white (not black)\n- Circularity\n\nStar: fill ratio ~0.3-0.5, no hole.\nFilled circle: fill ratio ~0.7-0.8, no hole.\nOpen circle: fill ratio ~0.5-0.7, has hole.\n\nHmm, open circle and star might be confused. Let me use the hole test: open circles have a clear white center. Stars don't (they're filled in the middle).\n\nLet me implement this.\n\nActually, the stars in this plot look like they have a slight hollow? Let me check. From the montage, the stars look solid (filled). The open circle clearly has a white center. So:\n- Hole present → open circle (EuZn₂Sb₂)\n- No hole, high fill, round → filled circle (EuCd₂Sb₂)\n- No hole, lower fill, spiky → star (YbZn or YbCd, by y position)\n\nLet me implement this."}}
