en_star: center \"#####.#####\" has a white dot, and \"##..#\" \n   - filled_star: center \"###########\" solid\n\n   So the number of white pixels in the center region distinguishes open from filled.\n\n2. **Circle vs Star**: \n   - Circle: the top is rounded (wide at top-middle: \"...#####...\"), symmetric left-right, roughly circular.\n   - Star: has a single point at the very top (\".....#.....\"), narrow at top, then widens. The star has a distinctive top point.\n   \n   A good feature: the width at the top row of the marker. For a star, the topmost black pixel is a single point (width ~1-2). For a circle, the topmost is a wider arc (width ~5).\n   \n   Or: the vertical extent vs horizontal extent ratio. Stars are taller (the points extend vertically).\n   \n   Or: the number of \"arms\". \n\nLet me use a simpler approach. Let me measure:\n- `center_white`: fraction of white pixels in a central cross/region → high for open, low for filled.\n- For circle vs star: measure the width of the topmost black row within the marker. Star → narrow top (1-3 px), Circle → wide top (4-6 px).\n\nActually, let me look at a cleaner discriminator between circle and star:\n- Circle: the marker's leftmost and rightmost extents are at the MIDDLE row (widest in middle). The top and bottom are narrower (rounded).\n- Star: the widest part is at the middle (the two side points), but there are ALSO points at top and bottom.\n\nHmm, both circle and star are widest in the middle. \n\nBetter: Look at the TOP of the marker:\n- Circle top: a broad arc, like \"#####\". The top row has ~5 black pixels.\n- Star top: a narrow point, like \"#\". The top row has ~1 black pixel.\n\nLet me measure the width of black pixels in the topmost 2 rows of the marker (the rows that contain the highest black pixel). \n\nLet me code a classifier:\n- For a marker at (cx, cy), look at a 11x11 window.\n- Find all black pixels.\n- `filled` = (center pixel region mostly black). Let me count white pixels in a 5x5 center box. Open → more white.\n- `star` vs `circle`: count black pixels in the top region (the topmost 1-2 rows of the marker's bounding box). Star has fewer (point), circle has more (arc).\n\nLet me also consider: open_star and filled_star both have the top point. Circle (open/filled) both have the top arc.\n\nLet me code and test on the 4 legend markers, then apply to all black markers in the plot.\n\nActually, the cleanest and most reliable: I'll detect all black markers (via erosion + connected components, merging near ones), and for EACH one, render a small window and classify by:\n- center_fill (open vs filled)\n- top_width (star vs circle)\n\nLet me define these carefully and test on legend. Let me write the classifier with good features."}}
