lob at cx=137 (size 96) is between 129 and 143. So yes, the blue \"137\" point is actually TWO points merged: one at ~129 (350K) and one at ~143 (375K).\n\nHmm wait, but that would make the blue series have points every 25K: 300,325,350,375,400,...,700. That's 17 points (300 to 700 in steps of 25). Let me count blue: 300,325,350,375,400,425,450,475,500,525,550,575,600,625,650,675,700 = 17 points.\n\nThe detected blue points (excluding legend at 91,46):\n101(300), 115(325), [137 = merged 350+375], 157.5(400), 171.6(425), 185.6(450), 199(475), 213.6(500), 228(525), 242(550), 256(575), 270(600), 284.5(625), 300(650), 312.3(675), 326.4(700).\n\nSo blue = 15 distinct detected blobs, one of which (137) is a merged pair → 16? No wait. Let me recount: 101,115,137,157.5,171.6,185.6,199,213.6,228,242,256,270.1,284.5,300,312.3,326.4 = 16 blobs. If 137 is two merged points (350 & 375), then total = 17 points. That matches 300-700 step 25 = 17 points. \n\nBut wait, the gap from 115 (325K) to 157.5 (400K) is 42 px = 75K, which should be 3 points apart (325, 350, 375, 400). So yes, the merged blob at 137 represents the 350 and 375 points. So blue has 17 data points.\n\nHmm, but actually maybe it's not 25K steps. Let me reconsider. Let me re-examine. Actually, maybe the data is at 300, 325, 350, 375, ... OR maybe the points are irregular. Let me look at the actual marker positions more carefully by detecting individual marker centers even when they overlap.\n\nActually, this is getting complex. Let me reconsider the whole approach. This is a dense plot with 6 curves and ~17 points each. The black curves (4 of them) are overlapping in the lower region. This is genuinely hard.\n\nLet me take a step back and think about the ground truth. This looks like a figure from a paper on skutterudite/thermoelectric compounds (EuZnCdSb etc). Actually the compounds EuZn₁.₈Cd₀.₂Sb₂, YbCd₁.₆Zn₀.₄Sb₂, EuZn₂Sb₂, EuCd₂Sb₂, YbCd₂Sb₂, YbZn₂Sb₂ — these are ZnSb2-based thermoelectrics. The figure shows zT