{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_373","type":"reasoning","text":"Now I can see the ordering in the right region (high T, x 230-360):\nFrom top to bottom at the right side:\n- Blue stars (top, YbCd₁.₆Zn₀.₄Sb₂)\n- Red circles (EuZn₁.₈Cd₀.₂Sb₂) — wait, blue is above red here?\n\nLet me look again. In the right region:\n- Top: blue star at top right (the highest point ~y small)\n- Then red circles\n- Then black open circles (hollow)\n- Then black open stars (hollow) and black filled circles — these are intertwined\n- Then black filled stars (bottom)\n\nWait, the red is BELOW blue in the right region. Let me re-examine. Looking at the image: the blue stars go highest (top-right corner), then red circles are below them, then the black curves below.\n\nSo at high T, blue > red. But at low T (left), red was above blue. So they cross!\n\nLet me re-examine the full picture. Actually this is a classic thermoelectric zT plot. Let me carefully map each curve.\n\nLet me now focus on the systematic approach. I'll detect each marker by color and by shape.\n\nRed markers: filled circles, red color — easy.\nBlue markers: stars, blue color — easy.\n\nThe 4 black series need shape-based separation:\n- Black open circles (hollow) — EuZn₂Sb₂\n- Black filled circles — EuCd₂Sb₂\n- Black open stars (hollow) — YbCd₂Sb₂\n- Black filled stars — YbZn₂Sb₂\n\nDistinguishing features:\n- Circle vs star: circle is round, star is 5-pointed\n- Open (hollow) vs filled: hollow has white center, filled is solid black\n\nLet me detect black markers and classify each by:\n1. Is it hollow? (has white center)\n2. Is it a circle or star? (shape)\n\nThis is complex but doable. Let me first get all black marker blobs (connected components of black) in the data region, excluding the legend, axis lines, and connecting lines.\n\nActually, the markers are connected by lines, so connected components will merge markers+lines. I need a different approach.\n\nBetter approach: For each black marker, the mark