xels into a single blob per marker, then classify each blob. The key insight is that circles have small bounding boxes (roughly square) while stars are wider, and hollow markers have a white interior while filled ones don't. I can use the area-to-bounding-box ratio plus hole detection to reliably separate them.\n\nLet me work through a single column first to calibrate the classification logic.\n\nWriting classification script..."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_377","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"cd /home/mato/.cache/real-chart-bench/codex-local/work/pixcal/qwen3.8-27b/part6 && python3 << 'EOF'\nfrom PIL import Image\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import ndimage\nim=Image.open('images/fig_093.png').convert('RGB')\na=np.array(im)\nH,W,_=a.shape\nr,g,b=a[:,:,0].astype(int),a[:,:,1].astype(int),a[:,:,2].astype(int)\nblack=(r<90)&(g<90)&(b<90)\n# remove axis frame lines: the frame is at x=72 (left), x=355 (right), y=20 (top), y=230 (bottom)\n# Also remove tick marks. We'll handle by working only in the inner data region.\n# Data region inner: x in [74,354], y in [21,229]\n# Also remove the legend box. Determine legend box: x in [76,205], y in [21,152]?\n# Let's just build masks with legend excluded for now.\n\n# Expected x grid (px)\nxs_grid = [round(100.8 + (T-300)/400*226.05,1) for T in range(300,701,25)]\nprint('x grid px:', xs_grid)\n\n# For each x in grid, look at black pixels in column band [x-6, x+6]\n# Find connected components (dilate to merge marker parts)\nfor xp in xs_grid:\n    x0=int(xp-6); x1=int(xp+6)\n    band = black.copy()\n    band[:, :max(0,x0)] = False\n    band[:, min(W,x1+1):] = False\n    band[:21,:] = False\n    band[230:,:] = False\n    # dilate to connect\n    dil = ndimage.binary_dilation(band, iterations=1)\n    lab,n=ndimage.label(dil)\n    blobs=[]\n    for i in range(1,n+1):\n        ys,xs=np.where(lab==i)\n        if len(ys)<6: continue\n        # restrict to near center x (marker core within 5px)\n        # compute extent\n        y0,y1=ys.min(),ys.max(); x0b,x1b=xs.min(),xs.max()\n        cy=ys.mean(); cx=xs.mean()\n        # only keep blobs whose cx is near the column center (within 5)\n        if abs(cx-xp)>5: continue\n        # hole: white pixel inside the bbox that is enclosed\n        sub_orig = black[y0:y1+1, x0b:x1b+1]\n        sub_white = (not black)[y0:y1+1, x0b:x1b+1]\n        # count white in bbox\n        white_in = sub_white.sum()\n        # hole detection: label white within bbox, see if any not connected to bbox border\n        # simple: check center pixel\n        ch = (y0+y1)//2; cw=(x0b+x1b)//2\n        center_white = not black[ch,cw]\n        blobs.append((round(cy,1), round(cx,1), len(ys), int(y1-y0+1), int(x1b-x0b+1), int(white_in), bool(center_white)))\n    blobs.sort()\n    print(f'--- x={xp} ---')\n    for bl in blobs:\n        print('  cy,cx,size,h,w,whiteIn,centerWhite:', bl)\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
