{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_817","type":"reasoning","text":"Let me write a vectorized version. For each candidate center (cx, cy) on the grid, we need the proportion of white/dark pixels within a radius band. We can precompute it as follows: for each candidate center, use a fixed window (e.g., 7x7, 9x9, 13x13) and a precomputed radius mask.\n\nApproach:\n- For a given cx (integer or half-integer), and a list of cy candidates, extract the window a[cy-R:cy+R+1, cx-R:cx+R+1] as a white array.\n- Precompute radius masks for integer centers within a window of radius R=6 (i.e., a 13x13 patch): for a 13x13 patch centered at (6,6), the disk r<1.5, disk r<2.2, ring 2.4-4.6, ring 3-6, disk 3.2, annulus 2.5-6.5.\n- Then, for each cy, take the patch and compute the mean over the mask.\n\nSince cy varies by 0.5, the center can be at an integer or half-integer position. If we use an even-sized patch (e.g., 14x14) and compute the center pixel as the (7,7)/(7,8) average... an easier way: evaluate only at integer cy positions. Markers in the figure are probably at integer pixel positions (or half-positions). The precision of 0.5 px in y corresponds to ZT 0.0035, so an integer cy is sufficient.\n\nSo: for each grid column cx (integer), for each integer cy in 20..226:\n- Patch P = white[cy-6:cy+7, cx-6:cx+7] (13x13)\n- Precompute masks M_disk15 (pixels with dist<1.5 from center (6,6)), M_ring245 (2.4<=d<=4.6), etc.\n- c2 = P[M_disk2].mean(), etc.\n\nThis is fast: 17 columns × 207 cy × a few mask operations on 13x13 patches. No problem.\n\nAlso, regarding the shape (circle vs star) of the open marker: ring245 is high for both open circles and open stars (the star's arms cross that ring, but not all of it). Distinguishing feature: for an open star, the dark fraction of the ring is lower (the arms cover about 6 out of the 360°... actually the arms are thin, so the dark fraction of the ring 2.4-4.6 might be 0.3-0.5). For an open circle: about 0.7-0.9.\n\nFor filled star vs filled circle: disk3 is high for a filled circle (about 0.9), lower for a filled star (about 0.6-0.75).\n\nLet me rewrite this vectorized."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_818","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"cd /home/mato/.cache/real-chart-bench/codex-local/work/pixcal/qwen3.8-27b/part6 && cat > zz93_score2.py <<'EOF'\nimport numpy as np\nfrom PIL import Image\na = np.array(Image.open('images/fig_093.png').convert('RGB')).astype(int)\nr,g,b = a[:,:,0],a[:,:,1],a[:,:,2]\nwhite  = (r>160)&(g>160)&(b>160).astype(bool)\nwhite  = white & (g>160) & (b>160)\ndark   = ~white\nH,W = a.shape[:2]\n\nR = 6\nyy,xx = np.mgrid[-R:R+1,-R:R+1]\nd = np.sqrt(xx*xx+yy*yy)\nM = {\n 'c15':  d<1.5,\n 'c22':  d<2.2,\n 'r245': (d>=2.4)&(d<=4.6),\n 'r36':  (d>=3.0)&(d<=6.0),\n 'd32':  d<3.2,\n 'a26':  (d>=2.5)&(d<=6.5),\n}\n\ndef feats(cx,cy):\n    Pw = white[cy-R:cy+R+1, cx-R:cx+R+1]\n    Pd = dark[cy-R:cy+R+1, cx-R:cx+R+1]\n    f = {}\n    for k,mk in M.items():\n        f[k] = Pw[mk].mean() if k in ('c15','c22') else Pd[mk].mean()\n    return f\n\ndef scores(f):\n    oc = (f['r245']*0.9 + f['c22']*0.3) if (f['c22']>=0.45 and f['d32']<0.75) else -1\n    ost= (f['r36']*0.7 + f['r245']*0.3 + f['c15']*0.3) if (f['c15']>=0.4 and f['d32']<0.8) else -1\n    fil= f['d32']\n    return oc,ost,fil\n\ngridx = [100.8 + k*(326.85-100.8)/16 for k in range(17)]\ngridT = [300+25*k for k in range(17)]\ndef px2y(py): return (py-222.7)*(1.4)/(19.95-222.7)\n\nfor cx,T in zip(gridx,gridT):\n    cx=int(round(cx))\n    cands=[]\n    for cy in range(22,226):\n        f = feats(cx,cy)\n        oc,ost,fil = scores(f)\n        cands.append((max(oc,ost,fil*0.9), cy, f['c22'], f['r245'], f['r36'], f['d32']))\n    # local maxima\n    cands.sort(key=lambda z:-z[0])\n    top = cands[:14]\n    print(f\\\"T={T}: \\\" + \\\" | \\\".join(f\\\"y={cy} w{c22:.2f} r{r245:.2f} s{r36:.2f} d{d32:.2f}\\\" for _,cy,c22,r245,r36,d32 in top))\nEOF\npython3 zz93_score2.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
