ets pulled up. The actual red circle at 300K is at py≈193 (0.18). So the red centroid 140.1 is a mix of legend line pixels (y≈29) and the marker (y≈193). Damn.\n\nSimilarly the blue strip at T=300 (x 96-106): the legend's blue line reaches x≈99 at y≈46 → the blue centroid 165.4 is also contaminated (true value ≈195? 0.185).\n\nSo I have to exclude the legend region for red/blue too. Legend box: x 84-170, y 14-128.\n\nLet me redo it: define the legend rectangle: x0=84, x1=170, y0=13, y1=130. Exclude from all detections (red, blue, dark, white holes).\n\nBut wait — are there any real data points inside the legend rectangle? The legend occupies the upper-left; the data curves rise toward the upper-right. At T=300-450 (px 101-186), the max ZT of any series is red at 450 = 0.54 → py = 222.7-0.54*144.8=144.6 → outside the legend (y>130). At px 170-186 (T≈425-450), the legend's x1=170, so only a small overlap; red at 450 is py 144.6 > 130 → no problem. Blue at 450 is 0.45 → py 157. No problem. So excluding the legend rectangle is safe.\n\nNow, about the blue series values — after excluding the legend, blue at 300 should be about 0.185, not 0.3956. Let me recompute.\n\nAlso red at 300: 0.18? Both red and blue are about 0.19-0.2 at 300K (red slightly above blue? From the image at 300K, red circle about 0.20, blue star about 0.185).\n\nOK, let me rewrite it with the legend exclusion, and for black output per-candidate features (window fr, h, core_n, hole presence, hole area) so I can assign series reliably. Also let me compute legend calibration for filled circle vs star: window fr of legend filled circle=0.60 vs filled star=0.4625; open circle h=6 vs open star h=8.\n\nClassification rule v2:\n- Open: has hole. Circle: window h ≤ 7 (or fr ≥ 0.55); star: h ≥ 8.\n- Filled: no hole. Circle: window fr ≥ 0.55; star: fr < 0.55.\n\nRisk: when a filled circle overlaps with the red/blue (the top of the circle is hidden), fr drops below 0.55 → misclassified as star. Mitigation: use erosion core size: circle core is compact (n_core ≥ 8?), star core is smaller (≤7)? From T=300: circle core 13, star core 5. Let me compute the legend cores: erode the legend circle and star and measure.\n\nLet me also double-check the \"hole\" classification of open star vs open circle: legend open circle window h=6, open star h=8. Rule h≥7.5 → star.\n\nNow, the overlapping pair in the middle range (filled circle about 0.49 and open star about 0.48 at 550): one has a hole → open star; the other doesn't → filled circle. Good, that resolves it if both are detected. At 550 in extract2, only 2 cores, no holes — the open star's hole was filled in? If the filled circle overlaps the open star, the ring's hole gets covered by the black fill → no white hole → both look filled. Then classification by fr: the combined blob is large and fr is intermediate. Ugh.\n\nAlternative for ambiguous columns: use series continuity! I know the general shape:\n- Filled circle (EuCd2Sb2): monotonic, roughly from 0.11 (300K) to 0.68 (700K)? In fact, at 700K filled circle ≈0.68 (from the image: black filled dot at about 0.68 at 700K, below the 0.98 open star).\n- Open star (YbCd2Sb2): from about 0.08 (300K) to 0.98 (700K) — crosses over the filled circle between about 600-650K.\n- Open circle (EuZn2Sb2): from about 0.10 (300K) to about 0.87 (650K), ends at 650 (13 points, 300..650).\n- Filled star (YbZn2Sb2): from 0.03 (300K) to 0.47 (700K), 17 points.\n\nLet me verify the open circle series length: from the tr12 zoom: the open circles are …, 600 (0.81), 625 (0.85), 650 (0.87) — then at 675/700 there are no open circles, only stars. And in the earlier full 10x: the open circles end at about 650. So 13 points.\n\nFilled circle at 675? From the image at 675K: open star about 0.9, filled circle about 0.62?, filled star about 0.42. In the tr12 zoom (region 270-360 x, 30-120 y): visible are: red circles (600, 625, 650), blue stars (600, 625, 650, 675, 700), open circles (600?, 625, 650), an open star at about (675? 0.9), an open star at 700 (0.98), a filled star at 675 (0.42), a filled star at 700 (0.47). Hmm, where's the filled circle at 675/700? In the tr12 crop (270-360, 30-120 → ZT 1.07..0.41), the filled circle at 675 (0.62 → py≈133) and 700 (0.68 → py≈124) are below the crop. Let me zoom into that region specifically.\n\nLet me do a comprehensive re-extraction with the legend exclusion and full diagnostics, and zoom into ambiguous spots."}}
