\n\nHmm, I'm confused now. Let me look at the actual images at high zoom and carefully, column by column. That's the reliable path. The images are small (405x300), so each marker is only ~8–12 pixels. Let me zoom into each column individually at very high magnification and visually read the marker shapes.\n\nLet me generate single-column crops for the ambiguous middle region and inspect them.\n\nActually, given the handoff has already done a lot of this work, and the values are \"verified,\" let me focus on the truly unresolved questions:\n1. Where does the open circle start? (Is it at 425 or earlier?) — check 300–400 for a ring near the blue star.\n2. Open circle at 550 (hidden under the blue star) — fill in by trend.\n3. Filled circle at 675 (~0.70) and is there a point at 700?\n4. Open star at 300–525 (faint) — refine.\n5. Open star vs filled circle assignment at 550–700 (the crossover region).\n\nLet me look at the images I already have: zz93_t375_400.png, zz93_t425_450.png, zz93_t550.png, zz93_t650_700.png, zz93_t375_400b.png.\n\nzz93_t650_700.png (crop 290–342, 90–148): what I can see is:\n- Upper left: an open circle (a ring with a white center) — that's around 625/650.\n- Upper right: an open star (a star outline with a white center) — that's around 650/675, higher up.\n- Center left: an open star with a white center (around 625?).\n- Lower left: a filled circle (a solid black dot) — around 650?\n\nLet me look at it carefully. Crop x=290–342 (T≈642–708), y=90–148 (z from px2y(90)=0.915 to px2y(148)=0.515). So this window is the upper-right area.\n\nWhat I see in the image:\n- Upper left (~x=305, y=98): a ring (open circle) — white center with a black ring.\n- Upper right (~x=322, y=93): a star outline (open star) with a small white hole.\n- Middle left (~x=300, y=128): a star outline (open star) with a white hole.\n- Lower left (~x=296, y=137): a filled circle (solid).\n\nHmm, it's hard to map exactly. Let me do single-column high zoom. Let me write a script