ly, the handoff's \"675 ~0.70\" was a visual estimate. Let me check carefully.\n\nActually, let me rethink the entire upper region. There are several series in the upper region (z 0.5–1.0):\n- Open circles (EuZn2Sb2): 425:~0.41? ... 650:0.868\n- Open stars (YbCd2Sb2): 375:0.174 ... 700:~0.98\n- Red filled circles: up to 650 (1.061)\n- Blue filled stars: up to 700 (1.225)\n\nAnd the open circles (EuZn2Sb2) and open stars (YbCd2Sb2) are the two \"open\" black series. The filled circle (EuCd2Sb2) is a separate curve.\n\nLet me re-verify. Holes = open markers (open circles or open stars). Let me enumerate the holes:\n- T=325: hole z0.226 (ar2, tiny) — likely the blue star's center hole? No, the blue star is filled. Actually this small hole at 0.226... the blue star at 325 is z0.227. So the \"hole\" at 0.226 is inside the blue filled star (the small white gap between the star's arms). Not an open black marker. Ignore.\n- T=375: hole z0.177 (ar2, tiny) — near the filled circle at 0.212? Or... Actually 0.177 is a core at 375 (ar2). Confusing.\n- T=425: hole z0.260 (ar3) — near filled circle 0.281.\n- T=450: holes z0.481 (x2, ar2) and z0.288 (ar2).\n- T=475: hole z0.543 (ar9, h3, w4) — this is a real hole, open marker at 0.543.\n- T=500: hole z0.606 (ar6, h3, w3) — open marker at 0.606.\n- T=525: hole z0.668 (ar7, h3, w4) — open marker at 0.668.\n- T=575: holes z0.744 (ar4, h2, w3) and z0.571 (ar2).\n- T=600: holes z0.806 (ar10, h3, w4) and z0.633 (ar2).\n- T=625: hole z0.854 (ar12, h4, w4) — big real hole.\n- T=650: hole z0.868 (ar10, h3, w4) — big real hole.\n\nHmm, this is getting complex. Let me think about which open markers exist where.\n\nThe key insight: there are two open black marker series (open circles = EuZn2Sb2, open stars = YbCd2Sb2). Their holes will appear. Let me figure out each one's trajectory.\n\nFrom the handoff:\n- Open circles (EuZn2Sb2): 425:~0.41, 450:~0.47, 475:0.537, 500:0.601, 525:0.663, 550:~0.71, 575:0.742, 600:0.806, 625:0.851, 650:0.868 (end