at markers are where using the core (filled) + hole (open) structure.\n\nFilled (dark) cores per column:\n- T=300: 0.122 (filled circle), 0.039 (filled star)\n- T=325: 0.150 (filled circle), 0.046 (filled star)\n- T=350: 0.177 (filled circle), 0.053 (filled star)\n- T=375: 0.212 (filled circle), 0.177 (open star, ar2), 0.067 (filled star)\n- T=400: 0.247 (filled circle), 0.212 (open star, ar2), 0.081 (filled star)\n- T=425: 0.281 (filled circle), 0.095 (filled star) [hole 0.260 = open star]\n- T=450: 0.316 (filled circle), 0.115 (filled star) [hole 0.481=open circle, 0.288=open star]\n- T=475: 0.350 (filled circle), 0.136 (filled star) [hole 0.543=open circle]\n- T=500: 0.392 (filled circle), 0.157 (filled star) [hole 0.606=open circle]\n- T=525: 0.440 (filled circle), 0.184 (filled star) [hole 0.668=open circle]\n- T=550: 0.488 (filled circle), 0.212 (filled star) [no hole → open circle hidden under blue, open star overlaps with filled circle]\n- T=575: 0.530 (filled circle), 0.247 (filled star) [hole 0.744=open circle, 0.571=open star]\n- T=600: 0.571 (filled circle), 0.281 (filled star) [hole 0.806=open circle, 0.633=open star]\n- T=625: 0.619 (filled circle), 0.329 (filled star) [hole 0.854=open circle]\n- T=650: 0.675 (filled circle), 0.371 (filled star) [hole 0.868=open circle]\n- T=675: 0.419 (filled star) [no filled circle core, no clear hole]\n- T=700: 0.467 (filled star) [no filled circle core, no clear hole]\n\nWait, this is a problem. At 675 and 700 there are no filled circle cores, and no open star holes either. But the handoff says open stars extend to 700 (~0.98) and filled circles may extend to 675 (~0.70).\n\nHmm. Let me reconsider. At high T (625–700), open stars and filled circles cross. Let me rethink the assignment of the high-z holes.\n\nActually, I realize I need to look at the image more carefully. Let me display the column zooms. The issue is: at 625, 650, 675, 700, is the high-z marker (~0.85–0.98) an open circle or an open star, and is the